<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal June non-tradable goods inflation slows.</title>
<headline>Portugal June non-tradable goods inflation slows.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Non-tradable goods prices, mainly wages, rose 0.2 percent month-on-month in June, down from 0.5 percent the previous month, while tradable goods prices fell 0.7 percent, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said on Monday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of both sectors:</p>
<p>Tradable goods:</p>
<p>				    JUNE 97	MAY 97	JUNE 96</p>
<p>Month-on-month		 -0.7 pct     0.8 pct     -0.5 pct</p>
<p>Rolling 12-month average    1.4 pct     1.7 pct	2.1 pct</p>
<p>Year-on-year		    0.0 pct     0.2 pct	2.7 pct</p>
<p>Index (base 100 em 1991)    123.4	 124.3	  123.5</p>
<p>Non-tradable goods:</p>
<p>				    JUNE 97     MAY 97	 JUNE 96</p>
<p>Month-on-month		  0.2 pct     0.5 pct	0.6 pct</p>
<p>Rolling 12-month average    4.6 pct     4.6 pct	5.0 pct</p>
<p>Year-on-year		    4.1 pct     4.4 pct	4.7 pct</p>
<p>Index			     148.1	 147.8	  142.3</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
